# CI compliance and release path

Source of truth: `AGENTS.md` CI/CD section, `.github/workflows/`.

## Contributor PR (feature/fix)

- One package per PR when possible (`libs/partners/<name>/`, `libs/core/`, etc.).
- Do not change `pyproject.toml` or `uv.lock` without maintainer approval.
- Do not modify `.github/workflows/` on feature PRs unless assigned an infra task.
- PR title must follow Conventional Commits — see `.github/workflows/pr_lint.yml`.
- GitHub Actions must be pinned to full commit SHAs, not tags (`AGENTS.md`).

## Local gates (mirror CI before push)

```bash
# Package gate (engineer)
.cursor/scripts/pre_pr.sh libs/partners/<name> "type(scope): description"

# PR-level gate (DevOps)
.cursor/scripts/pre_merge_ci.sh --base master libs/partners/<name> "type(scope): description"
```

## Key CI workflows

| Workflow | When it runs | Purpose |
|----------|--------------|---------|
| `pr_lint.yml` | Every PR | Conventional Commit title |
| `check_diffs.yml` | PR | Lint + tests for changed packages |
| `integration_tests.yml` | PR / schedule | Network tests (API keys in CI) |
| `check_release_deps.yml` | Release PR + `pyproject.toml` | Deps must exist on PyPI |
| `check_versions.yml` | Version bumps | `_version.py` consistency |
| `_release.yml` | Manual (maintainers) | PyPI release |

## Release path

Deployment for this library is **maintainer-triggered PyPI release**, not app deploy. The onboarding kit stops at **merge-ready PR**; release is via `_release.yml` with `working-directory` and `release-version` inputs.

## Release PRs

- Title format: `release(scope): x.y.z`
- Run `/release-readiness` or `pre_merge_ci.sh --allow-deps` before merge.
- `check_release_deps.yml` validates runtime deps resolve on PyPI like end-user installs.
